WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
With all the moving parts for a bakery and a coffee shop,

00:04.000 --> 00:07.000
it's quite challenging to operate globally.

00:07.000 --> 00:11.000
We do have a pretty big operation, our roastery, which is here in Brooklyn.

00:11.000 --> 00:13.000
We also have our headquarters in Denmark.

00:13.000 --> 00:17.000
So we are coordinating a lot between multiple locations,

00:17.000 --> 00:20.000
a lot of large teams, a lot of different departments.

00:20.000 --> 00:23.000
And a lot of that is done in Notion.

00:23.000 --> 00:26.000
With our new upcoming opening in Chelsea,

00:26.000 --> 00:29.000
the critical path or the roadmap, we manage by Notion.

00:29.000 --> 00:31.000
And there's so many moving parts to this.

00:31.000 --> 00:35.000
Every week we have a huddle within the team, project managers, architects,

00:35.000 --> 00:38.000
and I manage all the punch lists via Notion.

00:38.000 --> 00:43.000
Actually, I was the worst in the team when we introduced Notion

00:43.000 --> 00:46.000
because I default to my old ways.

00:46.000 --> 00:49.000
I'm not going to say what my old ways are in managing things,

00:49.000 --> 00:51.000
which is a Google sheet.

00:51.000 --> 00:54.000
I'm also not the most tech savvy, but it is actually user-friendly

00:54.000 --> 00:58.000
when you start really looking into it and understanding it.

00:58.000 --> 01:02.000
And now you have that AI feature, which you just type what you want

01:02.000 --> 01:04.000
and then it makes it happen for you.

01:04.000 --> 01:07.000
Everything is so centralized and it's really easy to find things

01:07.000 --> 01:11.000
and really easy to contact people and really easy to track everything that you're doing.

01:11.000 --> 01:15.000
It does make it a lot easier to be collaborating with other team members.

01:15.000 --> 01:17.000
You don't go into an opening thinking,

01:17.000 --> 01:19.000
everything's going to be perfect.

01:19.000 --> 01:20.000
Something's going to go wrong.

01:20.000 --> 01:22.000
It's just all about being ready.

01:22.000 --> 01:26.000
Notion becomes the resource for truth for us

01:26.000 --> 01:28.000
because that's where we feed all the information

01:28.000 --> 01:30.000
and that's where we also pull the information from.

01:30.000 --> 01:32.000
And that's how we stay consistent.
